{% if slide_title %}
HEADER (draw exactly as written, in this order; skip a line that is absent):
{% if label %}
  kicker: {{ label }}
{% endif %}
  headline: {{ slide_title }}
{% if subtitle %}
  subtitle: {{ subtitle }}
{% endif %}
{% if core_hook %}
DECK NARRATIVE: {{ core_hook }}
{% endif %}
{% else %}
OBJECTIVE: {{ objective }}
{% endif %}
{% if slide_type %}
SLIDE TYPE: {{ slide_type }}
{% endif %}

COMPONENTS (place each one with its tag and ref, exactly once; code draws its content):
{% for l in node_lines %}
- {{ l }}
{% endfor %}
{% for comp in self_drawn %}
- {{ comp.component_id }} · {{ comp.kind }} · draw it yourself (no ref){% if comp.content_summary %}: {{ comp.content_summary }}{% endif +%}
  Data for {{ comp.component_id }}:
  {% for key, value in (comp.content_data or {}).items() %}
  {{ key }}: {{ value }}
  {% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
{% if layout_hint %}

LAYOUT INTENT - which regions carry weight and how the components relate. This is a
priority statement, NOT pixel coordinates: turn it into bands + a %/max split using the
LAYOUT GRAMMAR. If it conflicts with the grammar's rules, the grammar wins.
{{ layout_hint }}
{% endif %}

SIZING: give each node the room its shape needs (more items or longer text = more room).
grow (from the weight) on the band that holds the slide's main nodes; h="max" minH on a
Chart or diagram node; a Table sizes to its rows. Header sizes to content.
TEXT you write (header, labels): only the plan's words. Never write a number, a name or a
point that a node already shows, and no source line unless a component is a caption.

Output the POM XML for this slide - a single <Slide> element, no <Theme>, no
